# ISIDA Class Creation Standards

Apply these rules for every new class in `isida`.

- Every new class must implement `IDisposable` and include `public void Dispose()` with safe one-time cleanup (`_disposed` guard).
- If the class owns persisted data files, call the class save method from `Dispose()` by default (respect stage/validation constraints).
- Register every new class/service in `Common/IsidaEngine.cs` in correct places: `IsidaContext` property, initialization step order, and disposal chain.
- **XML-документация обязательна**: для каждого публичного типа, члена, метода, свойства и конструктора — добавить `<summary>`, для методов — `<param>` и `<returns>`; иначе CS1591. Примеры:
  - `/// <summary>Описание</summary>` — свойство, поле
  - `/// <param name="x">Описание</param>` `/// <returns>Описание</returns>` — метод
- Organize class code into meaningful `#region` blocks (initialization, state, core logic, file I/O, dispose, etc.).
- In `IsidaEngine` initialization, never use dependencies that are not initialized yet. If cyclic dependencies exist, use explicit secondary initialization methods.
- Prefer constructor/initializer-injected references over direct `*.Instance` access inside class logic.
- Keep thread-safety explicit for mutable shared state (`ReaderWriterLockSlim` or equivalent where needed).
- New logic must not break existing behavior: keep backward-compatible defaults and avoid changing unrelated execution paths.
- After edits: build `isida.csproj`, fix any introduced warnings/errors, and ensure disposal/init order is still valid.

## Перед завершением

- [ ] Все публичные члены имеют XML-комментарии (иначе CS1591)
